      "description": "Broad Reach Power was a Houston-based utility-scale battery storage and renewable-energy platform founded by EnCap Energy Transition in 2019. Apollo-managed infrastructure funds collectively acquired a 50% stake in December 2021 alongside the EnCap-led shareholder group. Apollo confirms that Apollo Infrastructure Opportunities Fund II participated, but its individual allocation was not publicly disclosed. EnCap and Apollo announced the sale of Broad Reach Power's battery-storage business to ENGIE in August 2023, excluding 1.8 GW of solar and wind projects and 4 GWh of Mountain West battery projects from the transaction perimeter. ENGIE finalized its acquisition of 100% of Broad Reach Power from EnCap and Apollo in October 2023 and fully consolidated the acquired business. ENGIE's audited 2025 financial statements continue to report 100% ownership of Group Broad Reach Power, while EnCap classifies Broad Reach Power as realized in 2023. No current Apollo ownership or subsequent reacquisition was found through August 8, 2026. Public sources reviewed do not disclose the post-closing ownership or operating identity of the excluded Mountain West portfolio.",
